    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d853">

                <pb facs="0924" n="1758" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.711/2524</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-29T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8508. Your despatch 9275, June 7. Before Department determines its attitude
                    towards British decision regarding censorship of foreign diplomatic
                    correspondence in transit through England, please report present system of
                    transit of American pouches and whether carried by couriers from arriving to
                    departing steamers or entrusted to British postal administration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
